WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.386
I finished school at sixteen. The disease had already interrupted my last

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:10.222
year, and my examination results closed the medical school path I had expected.

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:20.658
During severe attacks I could not always keep down even water.

00:00:20.658 --> 00:00:25.642
Laboratory eosinophil counts became numbers I learned to anticipate from the pain.

00:00:31.258 --> 00:00:35.963
One week before a trip to the United States, an actual flare led

00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.667
to an endoscopy and a course of glucocorticoids. It was not preventive treatment.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:50.581
Clinical uncertainty turned into an accumulation of medications, tests, missed

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:55.195
days and attempts to understand what my own body was doing.

00:01:00.425 --> 00:01:04.416
I learned to investigate cells and materials while living with

00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:08.408
a disease whose symptoms could overwhelm even an ordinary day.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.645
The essay asks what disappears when a patient's life

00:01:16.645 --> 00:01:20.240
is reduced to a diagnostic label or a test result.
